{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Error Handling Validator",
  "description": "Validate proper error handling patterns with Either<Failure, T>",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "flutter_chat_app/lib/data/repositories/**/*.dart",
      "flutter_chat_app/lib/domain/usecases/**/*.dart",
      "flutter_chat_app/lib/presentation/bloc/**/*.dart"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Validate error handling implementation:\n\n**REQUIRED PATTERN: Either<Failure, T>**\n\n**Repository Layer:**\n```dart\n@override\nFuture<Either<Failure, User>> login(String email, String password) async {\n  // Check network\n  if (!await _networkInfo.isConnected) {\n    return const Left(NetworkFailure());\n  }\n  \n  try {\n    final userModel = await _remoteDataSource.login(email, password);\n    await _localDataSource.cacheUser(userModel);\n    return Right(userModel.toEntity());\n    \n  } on ServerException catch (e) {\n    return Left(ServerFailure(message: e.message));\n    \n  } on NetworkException catch (e) {\n    return Left(NetworkFailure(message: e.message));\n    \n  } on CacheException catch (e) {\n    return Left(CacheFailure(message: e.message));\n    \n  } catch (e, stackTrace) {\n    logger.e('Unexpected error', error: e, stackTrace: stackTrace);\n    return Left(UnexpectedFailure(message: 'Unexpected error: $e'));\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Use Case Layer:**\n```dart\n@override\nFuture<Either<Failure, User>> call(LoginParams params) async {\n  // Validate input\n  if (!_isValidEmail(params.email)) {\n    return const Left(ValidationFailure(\n      message: 'Invalid email format',\n    ));\n  }\n  \n  // Call repository\n  return await _repository.login(params.email, params.password);\n}\n```\n\n**BLoC Layer:**\n```dart\nFuture<void> _onLoginRequested(\n  AuthLoginRequested event,\n  Emitter<AuthState> emit,\n) async {\n  emit(const AuthState.loading(operation: 'login'));\n  \n  final result = await _loginUseCase(LoginParams(\n    email: event.email,\n    password: event.password,\n  ));\n  \n  result.fold(\n    (failure) {\n      logger.e('Login failed', error: failure);\n      emit(AuthState.error(\n        failure: failure,\n        operation: 'login',\n        retryAction: () => add(event),\n      ));\n    },\n    (user) {\n      logger.i('Login successful');\n      emit(AuthState.authenticated(\n        user: user,\n        isOnboarded: true,\n      ));\n    },\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**FAILURE TYPES:**\n```dart\n// Network issues\nNetworkFailure(message: 'No internet connection')\n\n// Server errors\nServerFailure(message: 'Server error: ${statusCode}')\n\n// Cache/Storage errors\nCacheFailure(message: 'Failed to save data')\n\n// Validation errors\nValidationFailure(message: 'Invalid email format')\n\n// Unexpected errors\nUnexpectedFailure(message: 'Unexpected error occurred')\n\n// Authentication errors\nAuthFailure(message: 'Invalid credentials')\n\n// Permission errors\nPermissionFailure(message: 'Permission denied')\n```\n\n**CHECK FOR VIOLATIONS:**\n\n❌ **Throwing exceptions instead of returning Left:**\n```dart\nif (error) throw Exception('Error'); // WRONG\nif (error) return Left(Failure(...)); // CORRECT\n```\n\n❌ **Returning null instead of Either:**\n```dart\nFuture<User?> getUser() // WRONG\nFuture<Either<Failure, User>> getUser() // CORRECT\n```\n\n❌ **Not handling all exception types:**\n```dart\ntry {\n  // ...\n} catch (e) {\n  // Too broad, should catch specific exceptions\n}\n```\n\n❌ **Not logging errors:**\n```dart\nreturn Left(ServerFailure(message: e.message));\n// Should also log: logger.e('Error', error: e);\n```\n\n❌ **Exposing technical details to users:**\n```dart\nServerFailure(message: 'SQLException: ...') // WRONG\nServerFailure(message: 'Failed to load data') // CORRECT\n```\n\n❌ **Not providing retry actions in BLoC:**\n```dart\nemit(AuthState.error(failure: failure)); // WRONG\nemit(AuthState.error(\n  failure: failure,\n  retryAction: () => add(event), // CORRECT\n));\n```\n\n**UI ERROR DISPLAY:**\n```dart\nBlocListener<AuthBloc, AuthState>(\n  listener: (context, state) {\n    state.whenOrNull(\n      error: (failure, operation, retry) {\n        final message = _getUserFriendlyMessage(failure, context);\n        \n        ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(\n          SnackBar(\n            content: Text(message),\n            action: retry != null\n                ? SnackBarAction(\n                    label: context.l10n.retry,\n                    onPressed: retry,\n                  )\n                : null,\n          ),\n        );\n      },\n    );\n  },\n)\n\nString _getUserFriendlyMessage(Failure failure, BuildContext context) {\n  if (failure is NetworkFailure) {\n    return context.l10n.errorNoInternet;\n  } else if (failure is ServerFailure) {\n    return context.l10n.errorServer;\n  } else if (failure is ValidationFailure) {\n    return failure.message; // Already user-friendly\n  } else {\n    return context.l10n.errorUnexpected;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**REPORT:**\n1. List all error handling violations\n2. Show correct patterns\n3. Suggest specific fixes\n4. Check if all failure types are handled\n5. Verify user-friendly error messages\n6. Ensure proper logging\n\nError handling is CRITICAL for user experience!"
  }
}
